WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.857
Sam Okafor: Hi all, I think we're all here. Linda, you're on mute. There you go.

2
00:00:13.857 --> 00:00:21.571
Linda Frost: Sorry! Hello. Yes, so lovely to meet you all. Is that a cat, Aiko?

3
00:00:22.571 --> 00:00:29.000
Aiko Tanaka: That's Biscuit, she goes where she likes. Hello!

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:38.929
Sam Okafor: Right, kickoff. Linda, what's the one thing that has to be true at the end of this?

5
00:00:39.929 --> 00:00:51.857
Linda Frost: The new site live before our open day on the 18th of January. We need it live by the 12th, so the receptionists can practise.

6
00:00:52.857 --> 00:00:59.929
Raj Menon: That's tight but fine if we have content by mid December.

7
00:01:00.929 --> 00:01:10.143
Sam Okafor: Budget is the fixed eighteen thousand pounds we agreed in the proposal, nothing on top.

8
00:01:11.143 --> 00:01:19.143
Linda Frost: Yes, eighteen thousand, and not a penny more, the partners were clear.

9
00:01:20.143 --> 00:01:27.786
Raj Menon: On design, I'll have three homepage concepts to you in two weeks.

10
00:01:28.786 --> 00:01:37.286
Linda Frost: Wonderful. Can you also look at the colours? The old site is very, very blue.

11
00:01:38.286 --> 00:01:44.786
Raj Menon: We can talk about that when you see the concepts.

12
00:01:45.786 --> 00:01:53.643
Aiko Tanaka: For copy I need photos of the team. Proper ones, not phone pictures.

13
00:01:54.643 --> 00:02:02.500
Linda Frost: I'll ask Marianne to organise a photo day, she looks after the rota.

14
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:15.143
Aiko Tanaka: Great. And I can write all the treatment pages, there are about thirty. Hmm, no, I can't do thirty by December on my own.

15
00:02:16.143 --> 00:02:23.286
Aiko Tanaka: Linda, could your team draft the basics and I polish them?

16
00:02:24.286 --> 00:02:30.929
Linda Frost: We'll see. Everyone is flat out until the new year.

17
00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:41.000
Sam Okafor: Okay, we'll come back to that. Contracts. I'll send over the contract addendum today.

18
00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:53.643
Linda Frost: Thank you. Oh, one thing, nobody knows who has the login for the domain. The old agency set it up and they've gone quiet.

19
00:02:54.643 --> 00:03:02.357
Sam Okafor: That's a problem, we can't point the new site anywhere without it.

20
00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:12.429
Raj Menon: Not sure the booking plugin will survive the move either, but that's a later problem.

21
00:03:13.429 --> 00:03:19.000
Sam Okafor: Raj, say more on that, is it a risk?

22
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Raj Menon: Honestly I don't know yet. It's a fifteen year old plugin and the new platform may not support it.

23
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:41.214
Linda Frost: Patients book online all the time. If that stops working in January, reception will have a nightmare.

24
00:03:42.214 --> 00:03:49.214
Sam Okafor: Understood. Let's leave that until Raj has looked at it.

25
00:03:50.214 --> 00:03:58.571
Aiko Tanaka: Sorry, you cut out, Linda, did you say the open day is the 18th or the 8th?

26
00:03:59.571 --> 00:04:04.000
Linda Frost: The 18th of January.

27
00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:11.714
Sam Okafor: Good. I think that's us. Thanks everyone, talk soon.

